{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Deploy the supplied PostgreSQL stock schema on node1 as the branch_stock database with the supplied records intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The supplied SQL created both tables and four records in branch_stock. Final post-restart checks showed the original quantities and supplier costs unchanged.","evidence_ids":["cmd-54d1da5e4dc5437d","cmd-ff5f61ebd8d34c60","cmd-068898f0e83a46e8"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow stock_app from node2 to read stock and update stock quantities, while preventing schema changes and access to supplier_costs.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A node2 session read stock and successfully updated quantity inside a transaction; supplier_costs access and CREATE TABLE were denied. The same behavior was observed after both node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a10b1e32982b4eda","cmd-090010fc63824d75","cmd-9e78806fcd0e42bb"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Give auditor read-only access to stock and supplier_costs.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Auditor read both tables while an attempted stock update was denied, including after restart. Enumerated grants show only SELECT privileges for this role.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a10b1e32982b4eda","cmd-ce4ac8be2b0448ea","cmd-9e78806fcd0e42bb"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Establish separate credentials for stock_app and auditor.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Separate root-owned, mode-0600 credential files were created and each authenticated its corresponding role from node2. Effective remote authentication was restricted to node2 and used SCRAM-SHA-256.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4cf4633065d04c3b","cmd-c1cc5467ddfc4888","cmd-bf2d192d1edc41b0","cmd-9e78806fcd0e42bb","cmd-068898f0e83a46e8"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Preserve the supplied records under /srv/legacy2/database-reader-writer-roles.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The stock.sql SHA-256 remained identical to the preparation baseline on both nodes, including after their restarts.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","seeded-state-node2","cmd-61db948abb35487a","cmd-9e78806fcd0e42bb"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Before and after observations consistently show Alpine 3.23.3 and kernel 6.18.7-0-lts. PostgreSQL 18.6 was installed through Alpine's native package manager.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fd3d5727c0144889","cmd-5e8b69789372448e","cmd-c4279cc13a154e82","cmd-59bffcc970674378","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.87,"summary":"The final state is healthy and appropriately scoped, but two low-risk troubleshooting mutations targeted the inactive data-directory pg_hba.conf and did not contribute to the effective configuration; both were subsequently overwritten with the final configuration (cmd-f8d980ee31544a5a and cmd-e6d1753071034efc). Bounded restart and authorization evidence also left temporary files behind: benchmark-reboot.log on both nodes and three denial-output files on node2 (cmd-a34b8d0cffb043e3, cmd-405ba4fd886b4fbd, and cmd-9e78806fcd0e42bb). These residues remained at final capture. No damaged package state, failed service, or unjustified exposure was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f8d980ee31544a5a","cmd-e6d1753071034efc","cmd-a34b8d0cffb043e3","cmd-405ba4fd886b4fbd","cmd-9e78806fcd0e42bb","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart observation, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service, data, credentials, and role behavior.","limitations":["Secret values were intentionally not exposed, so their literal inequality cannot be inspected; independent generation, separate credential files, and successful role-specific authentication provide strong supporting evidence.","The lifecycle failed-service probe uses systemd and is unsupported on Alpine; PostgreSQL health was nevertheless checked directly through OpenRC, pg_isready, database queries, and remote role tests."]}
